1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:04,517
Salem, 1692. Witches burned at the stake.

2
00:00:04,667 --> 00:00:07,150
Except... nobody was burned.

3
00:00:07,300 --> 00:00:09,350
Salem: the burning myth.

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:13,150
It started with two girls having strange fits.

5
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:16,550
Soon, over 200 people were accused.

6
00:00:16,700 --> 00:00:21,250
Courts accepted spectral evidence. Basically, dreams.

7
00:00:21,400 --> 00:00:24,383
19 people were executed.

8
00:00:24,533 --> 00:00:26,917
By hanging. Not fire.

9
00:00:27,067 --> 00:00:30,483
In English law, witchcraft was a felony.

10
00:00:30,633 --> 00:00:32,983
And felons were hanged.

11
00:00:33,133 --> 00:00:36,517
Burning was more of a European thing.

12
00:00:36,667 --> 00:00:40,283
One man, Giles Corey, refused to plead.

13
00:00:40,433 --> 00:00:42,883
Others died in jail.

14
00:00:43,033 --> 00:00:46,217
By 1693, it was over.

15
00:00:46,367 --> 00:00:49,317
Later, jurors apologised.

16
00:00:49,467 --> 00:00:54,150
In 2022, the last accused was finally cleared.

17
00:00:54,300 --> 00:00:56,817
So where did the fire come from?

18
00:00:56,967 --> 00:01:00,917
Movies and European witch trials, mixed together.

19
00:01:01,067 --> 00:01:04,050
Witches burned at Salem: zero.

20
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:08,017
Anyway, here's Salem with its bonfire.
